Lil Jon Announces New Memoir &#8216;I Only Shout So You Can Hear Me&#8217;: &#8216;Made Me Dig Deep & Turn&nbsp;Inward&#8217;

&#8220;You know, I can&#8217;t go back and ask my father that raised me, &#8216;Did you know?&#8217; It&#8217;s so many unanswered questions, and it just beats you up,&#8221; Jon says in a preview clip exclusively on Billboard . &#8220;And then you go through an array of emotions, of anger to frustration to sadness to doubt to &#8230; you don&#8217;t — it&#8217;s just everything you go through, and it&#8217;s just like your life is not what you thought your life is. And then it&#8217;s also like, well, what would my life have been like if I did know my other father? What would he have taught me? Or what would I have learned?&#8221;

He also spoke on losing his 27-year-old son , Nathan Smith, in an accidental drowning this past February while he was in the middle of writing this book and how his almost 2-year-old daughter Nahara helped numb the pain. &#8220;I didn&#8217;t realize I was gonna go through life-changing things while I was writing this book, like the loss of my son,&#8221; he said. &#8220;So, I think it was all divine timing with this book happening because these stories needed to be told.

&#8220;It&#8217;s been rough,&#8221; he added. &#8220;It&#8217;s been hard. It&#8217;s a bunch of things that have helped me get through it, like my daughter. You know, my daughter is almost 2 years old now, and, you know, having part of me ripped out of my chest, she was able to help to repair some of that. When I was cold, she was able to warm me up with her love.&#8221;

Nightline airs at 12:35 a.m. ET on ABC with episodes available to stream the next day on Disney+ and Hulu.

